Package: trota-artwork
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, plymouth, plymouth-label, plymouth-theme-spinner
Description: Trota OS artwork: logo, wallpapers, icons, boot splash
 Original artwork of Trota OS by TestardStudios: logo and wordmark in
 several variants, desktop wallpapers, application icons, the Plymouth
 boot splash theme and a GRUB theme.

Package: trota-release
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, base-files
Breaks: trota-software-sources (<< 1.0.1)
Replaces: trota-software-sources (<< 1.0.1)
Description: Trota OS release identification
 Installs the Trota OS /usr/lib/os-release through a dpkg diversion
 (ID=trota, ID_LIKE="ubuntu debian"). The original file of the base is
 preserved as /usr/lib/os-release.ubuntu and keeps being updated by
 base-files. VERSION_CODENAME/UBUNTU_CODENAME stay "noble" so that APT
 sources, PPAs and third-party repositories keep working. Also provides the
 python-apt templates for "Software & Updates" and the unattended-upgrades
 origins of the base archive and of Firefox, an APT pin that keeps snapd
 from being installed, and turns off the Ubuntu Pro advertising of
 "apt upgrade" and the background ESM/APT-news queries of ubuntu-pro-client
 (security updates are not affected).

Package: trota-software-sources
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, apt (>= 2.0), trota-release (>= ${source:Version})
Recommends: flatpak
Description: Trota OS desktop software sources
 Configures where the Trota OS desktop gets software that is not in the base
 archive:
  * the official Mozilla APT repository, so that Firefox is a .deb package
    updated by Mozilla (Ubuntu's transitional snap package is pinned away);
  * Flathub as the system-wide Flatpak remote, with a daily update of the
    installed Flatpak applications (trota-flatpak-update.timer).

Package: trota-desktop-settings
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, trota-artwork (= ${source:Version}), dconf-cli,
         gsettings-desktop-schemas, fonts-inter, yaru-theme-gtk, yaru-theme-icon
Description: Trota OS default desktop configuration
 GSettings and dconf defaults of the Trota OS GNOME desktop: dark style,
 wallpapers, dock, fonts, terminal colours, login screen logo and privacy
 defaults. Only defaults are changed: every setting remains user
 configurable. Gives the GDM sessions the Trota OS name (dpkg diversion of
 the ubuntu-session files) and keeps the desktop light: no file indexer, no
 GNOME Software or Ubuntu Pro notifier at login. A dpkg filter skips the
 Ubuntu wallpapers and the firmware files of data-centre hardware (Ethernet
 switch ASICs, SmartNICs, FastLinQ server adapters).

Package: trota-common
Architecture: all
Section: python
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${python3:Depends}, python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0,
         gir1.2-adw-1, trota-artwork (= ${source:Version})
Recommends: iproute2, pciutils
Description: shared library of the Trota OS applications
 Python modules shared by the Trota OS utilities: local system
 information, read-only diagnostics, APT catalogue queries, translations
 and GTK 4 / libadwaita helpers.

Package: trota-welcome
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${python3:Depends}, trota-common (= ${source:Version})
Recommends: trota-docs
Description: Trota OS welcome guide
 First-run guide of Trota OS: version information, quick access to
 settings, updates, documentation and support, and an overview of the
 preinstalled applications. Shown at login until disabled.

Package: trota-system-info
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${python3:Depends}, trota-common (= ${source:Version})
Description: Trota OS system information
 Shows the Trota OS and Ubuntu versions, kernel, architecture, CPU,
 memory, disks, graphics and network interfaces. Information is collected
 locally and never sent anywhere. Also usable from the terminal
 (--text, --json).

Package: trota-diagnostics
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${python3:Depends}, trota-common (= ${source:Version})
Recommends: network-manager, update-notifier-common
Description: Trota OS safe system diagnostics
 Read-only health checks: disk space, network, kernel, security features,
 system services, recent log errors and pending updates, with cautious
 suggestions. Nothing is changed or repaired automatically.

Package: trota-package-helper
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${python3:Depends}, trota-common (= ${source:Version}), apt
Description: Trota OS package search helper
 Searches the APT catalogue, shows essential package information and
 explains how to install software. APT remains the package manager: the
 helper never installs or removes anything itself.

Package: trota-docs
Architecture: all
Section: doc
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: Trota OS documentation
 Offline HTML version of the Trota OS documentation: installation,
 building, troubleshooting, security and licensing.

Package: trota-desktop
Architecture: all
Section: metapackages
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, trota-release, trota-artwork, trota-desktop-settings,
         trota-software-sources,
         trota-welcome, trota-system-info, trota-diagnostics,
         trota-package-helper,
         ubuntu-session, gdm3, gnome-shell, apparmor, unattended-upgrades,
         network-manager, update-manager
Recommends: trota-docs
Description: Trota OS desktop system (metapackage)
 Depends on all the Trota OS components. Removing it does not remove the
 rest of the system, but it should stay installed so that future Trota OS
 components arrive with normal updates.

Package: ubiquity-slideshow-trota
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Provides: ubiquity-slideshow
Conflicts: ubiquity-slideshow
Replaces: ubiquity-slideshow
Description: Trota OS installer slideshow
 Slides shown by the ubiquity installer while Trota OS is being installed
 (English and Italian). Self-contained HTML, no network access.
 .
 Ubiquity 24.04 also needs a slideshow to keep its privilege handling
 consistent during the installation.

Package: trota-server-settings
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, trota-release (= ${source:Version}), openssh-server, procps
Description: Trota OS Server, Edge and Cloud defaults
 Configuration of the headless Trota OS editions:
  * SSH with keys only (no root login, no password login unless enabled
    explicitly with cloud-init "ssh_pwauth");
  * a base set of kernel hardening settings (sysctl): kernel pointers and
    logs restricted, ptrace and unprivileged BPF limited, protected links
    and FIFOs, no ICMP redirects or source routing, SYN cookies;
  * bounded systemd journal, also on small edge devices.

Package: trota-kiosk
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, trota-server-settings (= ${source:Version}),
         trota-software-sources (= ${source:Version}), cage, firefox, adduser,
         fonts-noto-core
Description: Trota OS Kiosk and digital signage session
 Shows one web page full screen on the first screen, in Firefox (kiosk mode)
 inside the cage Wayland compositor: information screens, totems, menu
 boards, dashboards, self-service terminals.
  * starts at boot as the unprivileged user "kiosk", with a fresh profile
    every time; restarts by itself and once a day;
  * Firefox policies without update prompts, telemetry, password manager,
    developer tools or first-run pages;
  * page and console access set in /etc/trota-kiosk.conf, also with
    cloud-init for many screens at once.

